<.shell current={:email}>
  <h1>Email</h1>
  <p class="lead">An email address to reach someone by, with a copy button.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-sm">
    <dl>
      <dt>Email</dt>
      <dd><.email id="email-demo" email="sam.rivera@example.com" /></dd>
    </dl>
    <ul class="mt-4">
      <li><.email id="email-demo-1" email="president@example.org" /></li>
      <li><.email id="email-demo-2" email="training.officer@example.org" /></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    Any address people use to reach someone: a member's details, team admins, organization admins, SAR Duty admins, tax credit letters, and no-shows.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    An address that says who did something, such as "Decided by", or one inside a sentence or a message. Your own address, such as in the account menu. Write those as text.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.email id="…" email=&#123;member.email&#125; /&gt;</code>
    shows the address as a <code>mailto:</code>
    link, then a copy button, and breaks a long address anywhere. With no address it shows nothing, or the hint in <code>missing</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
